      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1badff2e6ad1e91e5872b413810218b852f5dac0eac40256077855471602e3f9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The common operation is a cutoff decomposition, but the cutoffs have source-specific meanings. In the Kadiri-style unit a cited finite RH verification excludes the candidate-zero case below T0 and leaves a uniform high-zero argument. In the reciprocal-square unit, computed zeros below t0 are subtracted from an upper bound for the full positive-zero sum at zero shift, while Lehman's test-function formula controls positive shifts. The later N(T) remainder supplies a different, uniform way to aggregate remote zeros. Finite information and analytic tails therefore complement one another without becoming a single certificate.",
