    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_65850d971401d5e42f507413a8d31d18c71d0f92ae2c15a9f493890acf130410",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The sources exhibit adjacent modules rather than a documented transfer of one paper's theorem into the other. Jutila converts zeros to large polynomial values, raises the detector to place its length in the range of a Halasz-Montgomery/reflection/fourth-moment estimate, and optimizes back to a density bound. Ramachandra separately derives a density estimate from F(s)M_H(s)-1, uses it to bound zero-contaminated logarithmic blocks, and on the retained intervals applies a Mellin-smoothed Dirichlet polynomial whose mean square reduces to coefficient-square mass.",
