    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_89dd133accfdf4ad879d72cde1c53033888cb82a17adcdfce97cc276026b6ca8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A sign change of the real critical-line Z-function gives a local lower bound on critical-line zeros, not completeness. Hutchinson's bounded verification closes that gap by matching at least 138 sign-change zeros with Backlund's independent total of exactly 138 zeros in the stated rectangle. The later Gram-block work changes only the order and cost of locating enough sign changes; it does not replace the independent total-count obligation.",
