    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b7896409c556ef0870a3c2f3879e06752a3139eeb988444934982e37e697de68",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The lecture-note chain first obtains cancellation in short sums of n^(-it) by Taylor polynomialization, Holder amplification, Vinogradov mean values, and controlled rational denominators; exponential blocking and Abel summation then insert n^(-sigma) and yield Richert's zeta bound near Re(s)=1. The notes state that this input is intended for an improved zero-free region, while the 2024 source supplies the common boundary representation 1-1/f(t) in which the classical and Vinogradov-Korobov envelopes can be compared. This is an input-to-target bridge, not a reproduction of the missing zero-free derivation.",
