    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e7ee50c2c07949ed9e50cb58529a467fd2646dcda70636b729ba7c10277fc8e2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The three searches expose two separate obligations: remain inside an admissible representation and evaluate candidates with the zero-free objective actually being claimed. The kernel families are each passed through Kadiri-specific checks before a reported R0 is obtained; the polynomial search exhibits a reversal between Landau's surrogate ordering and finite-R0 ordering; and the squared-modulus/autocorrelation coordinates enforce P_K(x)>=0 identically while leaving b_k>=0, b_1>b_0, and the R2 calculation as additional gates.",
