    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fb5ad609608d2e1cf32a8f917f70d4abc3c784a3d113657740ccd022b5cb06d7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The shared bridge is a nonnegative trigonometric average of logarithmic derivatives: Euler-product coefficients give a one-sided inequality while a putative nearby zero supplies a reciprocal-distance term. Harper closes an unshifted three-height version by combining local-disc growth with the exposed zero term; the Stechkin construction instead pairs rho with 1-conjugate(rho) and subtracts a shifted logarithmic derivative, so non-distinguished zero pairs can be discarded before the exceptional pair is bounded.",
